# Amendment #59 — workspace-sync α-hotfix: NN-resolved entries actually overwrite workspace files

2026-04-27. Critical bug-fix on Bundle α (#57, sealed `e619b6a`).
The α.1 NN ancestor-detection accept-canonical fast-path in
`merge_helper.py` set the verdict but never staged canonical's
HEAD content, so `apply_staging_atomically` silently no-op'd
on every NN-resolved path. Workspace files stayed at pre-apply
state while `state.yaml` advanced to "applied" — false-success.

Empirical reproduction (verified by primary persona 2026-04-27):
`pos-sync --workspace /Users/lukeivers/pos3 --auto-accept
--confidence-floor 0.85` against canonical at `44d470d`. Output
reported `applied: <ref>`; `state.yaml` advanced; audit showed
46 NN-resolved entries with `resolved_content_path: null`;
workspace files DID NOT match canonical's HEAD blob byte-for-byte.

Single locked decision (D-build.1) drives the surface:

  - **D-build.1** — restructure both NN branches (cache-hit at
    438-447, cache-miss at 495-504) so the verdict is set ONLY
    AFTER canonical's HEAD content is successfully read and
    staged. Read via a new helper
    `_read_canonical_blob_at_ref(canonical_path, ref, rel_path)`
    that wraps `git show <ref>:<path>` (mirrors the existing
    `_resolve_canonical_head_sha` shellout shape). Decode UTF-8;
    on `UnicodeDecodeError`, leave the entry PENDING so the
    legacy resolver path handles it. Call the existing
    `write_merged` callable (already wired by `cli.py`'s
    `_write_merged_to_staging`) to drop the content into
    staging. Set `entry.resolved_content_path` accordingly.

Surface added under `workspace-sync/`:

  - `src/workspace_sync/merge_helper.py` (EXTENDED, +~30 / -2 LOC)
    — `_read_canonical_blob_at_ref` helper (~15 LOC, mirrors
    `_resolve_canonical_head_sha`'s shellout pattern). Both NN
    branches (cache-hit + cache-miss) restructured to read +
    decode + stage before sealing the verdict. The
    `INFERRED_MERGED` write_merged path (line 575) is unchanged.

  - `tests/test_cli_b_shape.py` (EXTENDED, +1 test, ~80 LOC) —
    `test_alpha_hotfix_NN_resolved_paths_actually_overwrite_workspace_file`
    builds a real two-commit canonical (ancestor + HEAD), seeds
    a workspace with the ancestor's content, runs cli.main with
    `--auto-accept`, and asserts post-apply that the workspace
    file's bytes equal canonical's HEAD blob byte-for-byte
    (HC#4 binding — the file-content-on-disk assertion is the
    regression-test primitive that catches this bug class).

  - `tests/SEAL_COMMIT` advanced from `cd4c2f2` (#58 seal) to
    the amendment-#59 commit SHA via `pos-amend apply`.

  - `tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py` BASELINE bumped to
    the amendment-commit's HEAD~1 = `44d470d`.

Tests (workspace-sync — 1 new):

  - `test_cli_b_shape.py::test_alpha_hotfix_NN_resolved_paths_actually_overwrite_workspace_file` (1).

Backwards-compatibility verified (HC#2 + HC#3 binding):

  - All 139 existing #56 + #57 + #58 tests remain green at the
    amendment commit; post-hotfix total = 140.
  - The `INFERRED_MERGED` write_merged path (line 575) is
    unchanged. Bundle α's verifier-passes path continues to
    work via the same `entry.resolved_content_path` contract.
  - Class-A protection unchanged.
  - State.yaml / audit.yaml shapes unchanged (the only field
    that changes is `resolved_content_path` — pre-hotfix it
    was `null` for NN-resolved entries; post-hotfix it points
    to the staging file).
  - No new third-party deps (HC#5): subprocess + stdlib only.
  - Zero edits to `self-upgrade/`.
  - Zero edits to `workspace-bootstrap/`.
  - The `--canonical type=str` argparse shape from #58 is
    unchanged; the cli.py orchestration is unchanged.

Halt-trigger surface review (per plan-doc §10):

  #1 (other correctness gap exposed): FIRED — three findings
     surfaced as HALT-FOUND #1, #2, #3 in plan-doc §13:
       HALT-FOUND #1 — cli.py:271-274 `INFERRED_ACCEPT_CANONICAL`
         from the LLM resolver itself is also unstaged.
       HALT-FOUND #2 — cli.py:275-278 Class-B `ACCEPT_UPSTREAM`
         post-stage `clean_writes.append` never restages.
       HALT-FOUND #3 — `conflict_report.py` validator does not
         require `resolved_content_path` for
         `INFERRED_ACCEPT_CANONICAL`.
     All three deferred to follow-on amendment #60 per HC#1's
     named-scope binding. Owner ruling requested per plan-doc
     §11.
  #2 (performance): not fired — 46 paths × 1 git show ≈ 200ms
     is acceptable per dispatch.
  #3 (test setup harder than expected): not fired — existing
     `tests/conftest.py` fixture machinery composes cleanly.
  #4 (wall-time exceeds 2-3h projection): not exceeded.

Composition unlocked / repaired by this amendment:

  - The α.1 NN ancestor-detection fast-path now actually
    delivers its observable: workspace files match canonical's
    HEAD content post-sync.
  - The "milestone closed" claim from Bundle α's seal is now
    operationally true for the NN-resolved code path.
  - β.1's no-args `pos-sync` flow (sealed at #58) now produces
    a successful end-to-end sync against pos3 (where the bug
    was empirically reproduced) — pending follow-on amendment
    #60 closure of HALT-FOUND #1 + #2 for full coverage of
    the LLM-resolver `INFERRED_ACCEPT_CANONICAL` and Class-B
    `ACCEPT_UPSTREAM` code paths.
